        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Countries mark May Day with mass street demonstrations France Issued on: 01/05/2026 - 09:50 It is International Workers' Day, with activists around the world taking to the streets to demand higher wages, improved working conditions, and broader labor rights. In France, unions have called for demonstrations under the slogan “bread, peace and freedom,” connecting everyday worker concerns to ongoing conflicts in Ukraine and the Middle East. The day has also sparked a heated debate over whether employees should be permitted to work on one of the country’s most protected public holidays. World's largest sailing yacht christened in Saint Nazaire shipyards 30/04/2026 France Jean Lafaurie, 102 years old, still resisting 24/04/2026 Profile France France reaches its \"overshoot\" day 24/04/2026 France 24/04/2026 France Macron to host Lebanon's PM Nawaf Salam 21/04/2026 France France and Lebanon share 'cultural, religious and political links, dating back to the 19th century' 21/04/2026 Middle East A petition called 'Lebanon will not be the next Gaza' calls on French leaders to take action 19/04/2026 Middle East French right divided over primary vote one year from presidential election 18/04/2026 France Macron urges permanent reopening of Hormuz Strait 17/04/2026 France"
